# tools/hu_moments_witness.rish -- a labeling's SEVEN HU INVARIANT MOMENTS, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/centroid.rye reads a component's center (the first moment), image/moments.rye its
# orientation and eccentricity (the second moment about that center). Those still MOVE when a mark is turned or resized. This
# rung reads the fact that does NOT move: Hu's seven invariant moments (M-K. Hu, 1962), built from the normalized central
# moments up to order three so the seven numbers stay (near) constant under translation, rotation, and scale -- the fingerprint
# a shape classifier wants. Compose not braid: a SIBLING of centroid and moments, each reading the same pixels for a different
# fact; this rung owns the raw-moment accumulation and the closed-form invariants, and it derives the central moments about the
# TRUE centroid so a mark and its turned or mirrored copy match tightly.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a chiral right triangle (unequal legs) and its LEFT-TO-RIGHT MIRROR share invariants
# one through six exactly (they agree to 1e-16) yet carry i7 of OPPOSITE SIGN (i7 and -i7 to 1e-20), so the seventh Hu invariant
# tells a shape from its mirror image where no area, box, center, second moment, or orientation can. The same triangle turned 90
# degrees reads all seven invariants unchanged (i7 included -- rotation preserves it, reflection flips it); a symmetric plus is
# its own mirror so its i7 is exactly zero (the achiral control); the triangle scaled up 4x reads the same seven within the
# named discrete-rescaling residue; a single pixel reads seven zeros; an empty source refuses by name. No network, no key, no
# funds -- the turn-proof fingerprint of a mark a surface names the day it labels it, on our own open geometry.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/hu_moments_witness.rish

say "hu_moments: Language EN -- Season G invariant-descriptor reader over a LabelMap; hu_moments returns one HuSet per component, its seven Hu invariant moments (i1..i7) constant under translation, rotation, and scale, i7 flipping sign under reflection."
say "hu_moments: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: a sibling of centroid and moments, each reading the same pixels for a different fact; this rung owns the raw-moment accumulation up to order three and the closed-form invariants. No image written, no color, no codec."
say "hu_moments: Lens TAME -- the raw moments run in i64 (the largest, m30, under 2^59 for a full-image component) so a full-image accumulation can never wrap; the invariant slice is sized to the label count; an empty source refuses EmptySource up front so a refusal allocates nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/hu_moments"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/hu_moments.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "hu_moments: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "hu_moments: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "hu_moments: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-hu-moments" else "hu_moments: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "hu_moments: GREEN -- the chiral triangle and its mirror share i1..i6 yet flip the sign of i7 (the chirality no earlier reader can see), the same triangle turned 90 degrees reads all seven unchanged, the symmetric plus reads i7 exactly zero, the 4x rescaling holds within the named residue, a single pixel reads seven zeros, the refusal fires by name, on metal."
